---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Run Easy - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Run Easy iOS and watchOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/run-easy/privacy"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-12">Run Easy &middot; Effective October 22, 2026</p>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">The short version</h2>
            <p>Run Easy doesn't collect anything. Your runs, settings and health data stay on your iPhone and Apple Watch, and are never sent to us or anyone else.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Data storage</h2>
            <p>Runs, settings, goals and training plans are stored on your devices. Your iPhone and Apple Watch exchange runs and settings directly with each other. There are no accounts and nothing to sign up for.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Apple Health</h2>
            <p class="mb-3">With your permission, Run Easy reads your runs, heart rate, running form, steps, active energy and date of birth from Apple Health to set your MAF heart rate and show your training history. The Apple Watch app saves the runs you record to Apple Health as workouts and reads your heart rate during a run.</p>
            <p>Health data is used only on your devices. It's never sent to us, stored in iCloud by Run Easy, shared with third parties or used for advertising. You can change what Run Easy can read or write anytime in Settings &gt; Health on iPhone. If you don't allow access, the iPhone app still works with your age entered by hand.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Location</h2>
            <p>Only the Apple Watch app uses location, during outdoor runs, to measure distance and record your route. The iPhone app never asks for your location. Routes are stored with your runs on your devices.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Apple Music</h2>
            <p>If you turn on music controls in Settings, the Apple Watch app can play, pause and skip Apple Music on your iPhone during a run. Run Easy only controls playback; it doesn't read or change your library.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Analytics and tracking</h2>
            <p>Run Easy contains no analytics, no ads, no tracking and no third-party code that collects data.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Network use</h2>
            <p>Route maps are drawn with Apple Maps, which loads map images for the area of your run from Apple. Run Easy makes no other network requests.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Children's privacy</h2>
            <p>Run Easy does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under the age of 13.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page with the new effective date.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
